Casterwill was the original and first [[Seeker]] responsible for bringing the [[Titans]] to Earth from the [[Spirit World]], Huntik, in order to battle and defeat the [[Nullifiers]]. {{Source|All Work and No Pay}} At some point in the conflict, Casterwill called for the assistance of [[Cherit]]. {{source|Memory Lane}}

Casterwill took 500 years to defeat the [[Nullifiers]] and to seal the [[Spiral Mark]] with the [[Willblade]]. {{source|The Spiral Mark}} When he finally did so, Casterwill died right where he was standing. {{source|Coming of Age}} Lord Casterwill's legacy was passed on to his sons and daughters, who each received a Legendary Titan to fight against the [[Nullifiers]] if they ever return. {{source|The Spiral Mark}}

[[Cherit]] had a several dreams remembering his time at the side of Lord Casterwill. {{source|Memory Lane}} It later led him to discover the [[Golden Asp]] where the [[Ring]] of [[Tao]] was buried. {{source|The Golden Asp}}

Lord Casterwill appeared to [[Sophie Casterwill]] in the [[Crystal Caves]], signifying to her that she was a direct descendant of his. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}}

On [[Avalon]], Lord Casterwill's spirit appeared to [[Lok Lambert]] when he drew the [[Willblade]], knighting him and empowering him to invoke [[Pendragon]], the Legendary Titan of Champions. Although no one could remember the event, his spectral form watched [[Cherit]] at [[Dante Vale's house]]. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}

The statue of Lord Casterwill in the [[Fortress of Iron Will]] later disapppeared to awaken [[Titans]], [[Coralgolem]], [[Icarus]] and [[Feyone]] as they stormed into battle against the [[Blood Spiral]]. {{source|The Spiral War}}

Casterwill appeared to Lok again in the [[Inter-dimensional World]] at [[Tír na nÓg]], where he gave Lok the power to properly bond with [[Pendragon]]. {{source|Back Home}}

